  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 1234 AM MDT Mon Aug 3 2026\n\nWill keep this long term discussion short a sweet as there is not \nmuch to talk about with the synoptic set-up that will take hold over \nthe region. Starting off the long term period, Wednesday marks the \nday that the warm-up begins as ridging builds back in. This will not \nonly usher in warmer temps but block or hamper any moisture \ntransport into the region. Therefore, expect dry conditions with \nhighs topping out around 80 degrees F. As the ridge builds, so will \nthe heat as highs Thursday will climb back to near 90. Then the real \nheat makes a return Friday into next weekend as highs once again \nsurge into the upper 90s and low 100s, warmest across far eastern \nWyoming and the Nebraska Panhandle. As mentioned briefly, with the \nridge strengthening, don't expect much relief from any precipitation \nas we will remain dry heading into next weekend.",
